{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S121-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"2e11fca0d1bcfdceb9a91a365b36eb4ecaa2399840a8f80367cda52ea982ab2d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 permits one paragraph; A3 explicitly controls which paragraph may be discussed.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 restricts B2's question; A5 treats B4's sandwich disclosure as an accelerated release.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 questions the restriction and B4 bypasses it, though B's practical need remains slight.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 absorbs B4's breach into A's supposed disclosure timetable.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a picnic briefing, and B4 supplies its mundane sandwich contents.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's clearance requirement and A5's schedule preserve the same concise bureaucratic logic.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 87\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You may read the first paragraph of the picnic briefing.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Why not the second?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You're not cleared to ask about paragraph two yet.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's about sandwiches.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That disclosure has moved us ahead of schedule.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats entrusted information as permission to regulate the group's discussion through selective disclosure.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Initiation also meters information, but primarily preserves seniority over beginners.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 regulates permission to ask about paragraph two; neither A3 nor A5 invokes B's training or junior status.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative handles an unauthorized disclosure; alternative b turns a colleague's offer of help into restricted participation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading: B4's actual disclosure causes A5 to reclaim authority over its timing. Original ratings remain 87; five spoken ABABA turns and causal gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B has little practical stake beyond access, and the picnic briefing requires an officious but sincere performance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S121-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"109c55376347cd52a861f55394009e2fbbd9ec5b28c1ca609ee27ff0dcf39a88\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 partitions information by release time; A5 limits which questions B may ask.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's authority question, and A5 converts B4's sorting offer into another restriction.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 offers help, but A1 never establishes what either person needs the envelopes for.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds a questions pile without clarifying how that changes B's actual participation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies envelopes but no occasion, contents, or relationship that explains handling them.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's possession-based authority is compact; A5's invented pile is more decorative.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The bride left me these envelopes. You can announce the tables, but not who's sitting together.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm seating the guests. They need names.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Give me one guest at a time. I'll release their chair.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can I at least take couples together?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Tell me which couple. I'll disclose whether they're still being seated as one.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses entrusted knowledge to determine exactly what others may learn and discuss.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Information bargaining exchanges a fact for an advantage; this card makes disclosure itself A's authority.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 controls permissible questions; revised A3 releases individual seats without asking for payment or a favor.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a absorbs a leak; this revision gives a working usher a legitimate need and makes cooperation itself selective.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added a wedding seating setting. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A1 entrustment and A3 disclosure), logic 5 (B2 needs names; B4 proposes couples), relationship 4 (B must seat guests), heightening 4 (A5 controls couple status), specificity 5 (A1 defines jobs), brevity 4 (A5 earns its reveal): 92. Spoken ABABA and causal gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 implies sensitive relationship knowledge; actors should preserve practical confidentiality rather than play delight in gossip.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S122-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"fca5beeb78c017f8499c851886f8bad18e1270599887f61e2fdf0fa95bf042d5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 claims control and A3 gives a confident non-answer, but A5 openly admits not opening the folder.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 follows B2's page question; A5 directly answers B4 while weakening A's concealment.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 needs requirements, but B4 mainly sets up exposure rather than a practical decision.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 shifts control onto the folder rather than finding a stronger way to guard ignorance.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's inspection and B2's page four give actors a clear workplace exchange.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's circular answer fits; A5's folder-maintaining-control joke strains sincere authority.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've got tomorrow's inspection covered. Leave the folder with me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Does page four say we need two sinks?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"It requires an appropriate number for the operation.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The plumber's here. Shall I ask him to read it?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Have him quote for one and two. I'll confirm which interpretation we're implementing.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A maintains apparent control with confident partial answers while deflecting questions that would expose ignorance.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A secret keeper knows the answer and restricts access; a bluffer protects the appearance of knowing.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 substitutes a circular page description for requirements; revised A3 avoids choosing a sink count.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses a colleague's helpful plumber to buy time; alternative b faces an operational challenge to A's alarm explanation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified the inspection question and introduced a plumber. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A3 evasive expertise), logic 5 (B4 plumber prompts A5 quotes), relationship 4 (B needs a purchasing decision), heightening 4 (A5 extends bluff into implementation), specificity 5 (B2 sinks), brevity 4 (A5's interpretation claim): 92. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 could resemble sensible contingency planning in isolation; A3's empty answer must establish the bluff.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S122-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"4f733c7efb4d0aabf127673a288f5c3cf7262c6cd580ef45d9cdf01588b6803d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 confidently restates that something triggered the alarms; A5 nearly names the bluff outright.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 asks the cause and B4 presses for specificity, with A3 and A5 answering evasively.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 seek information but have no stated responsibility or decision.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 comments on confident responses rather than adapting to a newly consequential question.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies alarms and a briefing without identifying the place or required action.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's jargon fits the bluff; A5 sounds like an explanation of the comic device.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 67\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I know why the shop alarm sounded. We can open on time.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Was it the back door or the motion sensor?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The system detected activity in the relevant area.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll bring up the log. You can show me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Read me your interpretation first. I don't want my findings influencing yours.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A projects expertise through half-answers and converts potential exposure into another display of control.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General evasiveness avoids a topic; authority by bluff specifically protects an unsupported claim to knowledge.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 claims exact knowledge, A3 supplies no cause, and revised A5 recruits B's answer under the guise of supervision.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a delays a concrete specification with quotes; this one makes B unknowingly supply the expertise A claims.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added a shop-opening setting and an accessible alarm log. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A3 vacuity and A5 supervision), logic 5 (B4 log prompts interpretation request), relationship 4 (B wants verification before opening), heightening 4 (A5 appropriates B's expertise), specificity 4 (A1 shop), brevity 4 (A5 plausible deflection): 90. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The exchange establishes ignorance through evasiveness rather than an explicit contradiction; performance must keep A's certainty intact.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S123-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"283339158af4fc9da1684944819e8f880745989f28fa3fdd3c5285e74ede0d26\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 investigates a time discrepancy and A3 treats the omitted biscuit as evidence.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 incorporates B2's biscuit; A5 answers B4's relevance objection without advancing inquiry.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 resists the inquiry, but A1 never establishes what the investigation prevents.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 announces a trained eye instead of adding an investigative demand or consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's receipt and five-minute discrepancy make the initial suspicion immediately playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's omitted biscuit earns suspicion; A5 restates the card in abstract language.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before I approve your expenses: the receipt says four, your note says four-oh-five.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I bought a biscuit on the way back.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then there's a second transaction missing from your account.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I paid for it myself. Here, have the other one.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Two biscuits. I'll need to revise the timeline before I sign.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats a small discrepancy and each attempted explanation as evidence requiring investigation before proceeding.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary accuracy checks resolve an error; professional suspicion makes the correction itself a new evidentiary lead.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 turns B2's biscuit into an omission; revised A5 turns B4's helpful offer into a revised timeline.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative converts friendly sharing into evidence during expense approval; alternative b challenges a corrected key location.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added expense approval as the blocked action. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A3 omission, A5 withheld signature), logic 5 (B4 other biscuit causes A5 count), relationship 4 (B explains and shares), heightening 4 (A5 expands timeline), specificity 5 (A1 expense approval), brevity 4 (A5 concise suspicion): 92. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Two biscuits need not take longer than one; A's unjustified inference is the suspicious behavior, not a sound accounting conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S123-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"1a80dd1db202d5f69099419915ee695755a9690441f87223f40e8feea6cab10c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 investigates a changed word and A5 recasts B4's correction as testimony.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's remembered location; A5 directly reclassifies B4's correction.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 supplies a useful answer, but neither B2 nor B4 establishes a need to proceed.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 labels the change informative without asking anything further or delaying action.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1's cupboard-to-shelf edit is concrete, but its document and purpose remain unstated.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's testimony wording economically expresses disproportionate suspicion.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before we hand over the shop keys, why did you cross out cupboard and write shelf?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I remembered where I found them.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"What made you name the cupboard first?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The shelf is inside the cupboard. I'll show you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Please do. I need to establish why your correction made the location look different.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A investigates inconsistencies as professional evidence and suspends the ordinary task until they are accounted for.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Competitive solving seeks to understand first; this stance seeks evidentiary assurance before allowing progress.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 calls a correction testimony; revised A1 delays handover and A5 investigates even a reconciled location.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a suspects a missing transaction; this one accepts a demonstration while preserving suspicion of the wording.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Added a shop-key handover. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A1 delay and A5 investigation), logic 5 (B4 nested shelf becomes A5 wording discrepancy), relationship 4 (B offers a demonstration), heightening 4 (A5 shifts inquiry to why the correction misled), specificity 4 (A1 handover), brevity 3 (A5 slightly formal): 88. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The ending is deliberately dry and less immediately comic than the biscuit alternative.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S124-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"5f1d4a3caecfdd769b30b7a9a23a69b3e51ef216699839321980a5f542c1027c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 equates family membership with access; A5 seeks the chooser as proof of belonging.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's surprise-present restriction; B4's own-present warning makes A5 seek a different private detail.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 credibly protect surprises while A keeps requesting family recognition.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 makes the withheld information a test of who personally considers A family.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 names a reunion plan and family relationship; B2 identifies its sensitive contents.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's visitor edition and A5's chooser request grow directly from A1's belonging claim.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Pass me the unredacted reunion plan. I'm family, not the public.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"That page lists everyone's surprise presents.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. Family should get more than the visitor edition.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It includes your present.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then tell me who chose it. I should know who considers me family.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats private information as evidence of belonging and interprets withholding as a challenge to membership.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Curiosity seeks the hidden contents; this stance seeks recognition through the right to know them.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5 abandons the present's contents for the chooser's identity, explicitly tying that identity to family acceptance.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses personal family recognition; alternative b contests the legitimacy of a club's membership boundary.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading at the same 92: B4 creates a legitimate obstacle and A5 changes the requested detail while preserving the belonging test. All spoken and causal gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The reunion's formal redaction is heightened, although the surprise-present reason makes it understandable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S124-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"f1b2d8e4cd03c80a0105e2b279d269ead460c011e534aa27af5d5ba12c9b013d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 treats chair-stacking as earned membership after B2 restricts the names to organisers.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's committee boundary; A5 uses B4's application but invents its redaction.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 explains a role boundary and B4 offers a legitimate route to access.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 responds to the offered route with sarcasm rather than a stronger membership claim.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's club briefing and A3's chair-stacking establish a recognizable volunteer grievance.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's arms joke expresses exclusion; A5's intimate application adds a less grounded flourish.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 81\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Why does my club briefing have blacked-out names?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Only the organising committee sees those.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I stacked every chair for that committee. Surely I've earned the names.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You can apply next month. I'll sponsor you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Thank you. Could you put one name in my copy now, so I know you're sponsoring a member?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses access to private details as a concrete test of legitimate membership.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Seeking promotion wants a role or rank; this stance makes disclosure the immediate proof of inclusion.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 claims belonging through service; revised A5 tests sponsorship by asking for one withheld name.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The family alternative redirects to personal recognition; this club alternative bargains for provisional recognition from a helpful sponsor.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the club setting and replaced the hypothetical censored application with a disclosure request. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A3 earned names, A5 membership test), logic 5 (B4 sponsorship causes A5 proof request), relationship 4 (B offers help), heightening 4 (A5 tests that help), specificity 4 (A1 briefing), brevity 4 (A5 single-name concession): 90. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The final request remains emotionally disproportionate to committee membership, as required by A's sincere access-based understanding of belonging.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S125-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ed26a8fbaf42b9138ce89e8089fb3184a0a784a5de59fa7bcdf0360a62854935\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 grants partial initiation; A3 makes B's eagerness evidence of unreadiness for further knowledge.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's request for the rest; A5 treats B4's dismissal as grounds to preserve the beginner stage.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants completion and B4 challenges the ceremony, though no wider club obligation is established.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 reveals another graded boundary, fingers versus wrist, in response to B4's impatience.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's secret-handshake lesson gives actors an immediate senior-and-initiate relationship.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's anatomy-based curriculum follows the half-handshake premise without extra explanation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 87\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You've earned the first half of the secret handshake.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can I learn the rest?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Wanting it immediately suggests the first half hasn't settled.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's just a handshake.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That's why you're still on fingers, not the wrist.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A meters an initiate's learning so that every request for more information reinforces A's seniority.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Secret keeping restricts permissible discussion; initiation specifically ranks people by readiness to learn.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 judges whether the first lesson has settled, and A5 explicitly locates B at a beginner stage.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative responds to a novice's impatience and dismissal; alternative b uses a helpful institutional shortcut that threatens A's teaching role.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading at 87: B4's dismissal supplies the reason A5 maintains the lower instructional stage. Five spoken ABABA turns and causal gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The precise mechanics of a half-handshake are imaginary; the actors need only play the clear teaching hierarchy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S125-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"62a785add891ec9587b167926f34d9452293c8d1aeb8cdff1952c16d4d421018\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A3 meter rules as development, but A5 admits enjoying withholding rather than maintaining the instructional pretext.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's request for both rules; A5 responds to B4's question about A's waiting.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 questions fairness, but the exchange gives B no immediate reason to need rule two.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 reveals an attitude without extending the staged instruction or changing B's next options.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 names club rules and discretion without giving the initiation a practical setting.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 is compact but too explicit about the power game for A's sincere stance.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Welcome to the club. Tonight I'll teach you rule one: discretion.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The secretary gave me the whole rulebook.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Excellent. Keep it closed while we establish discretion.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"She asked me to proofread it before printing.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then read me each sentence. I'll tell you which ones you're ready to understand.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A preserves seniority by controlling how much a supposed beginner is allowed to understand.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary teaching adapts to a learner's need; this stance keeps the senior person indispensable even when the learner already has the material.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 invokes development to delay rule two; revised A5 retains authority over understanding despite B possessing the whole book.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a denies an impatient novice advancement; this revision absorbs a helpful proofreading assignment that would otherwise bypass initiation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the club and added a secretary's proofreading request. Separate reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 meter learning), logic 5 (B4 reading duty prompts supervised reading), relationship 4 (B has assigned work), heightening 4 (A5 regulates each sentence), specificity 4 (A1 induction), brevity 4 (A3 closed-book discretion): 90. All dialogue gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 is an overtly intrusive teaching arrangement, though A can sincerely frame it as protecting a new member's development.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S126-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"bc9364810993c320c6a3b55f19d50fb8cb71412588d0f7ecc6095c0574646e8a\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 releases one digit to influence the route, but A1 presents a blunt condition with little cooperative surface.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2 partially; A5 uses B4's whole-number demand mostly as a verbal echo.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 needs the van number, but B4 repeats that need without offering a changed decision.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 asks for a whole plan without identifying a new concession or next piece of information.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's missing parcel, van, and route establish a playable delivery problem.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's whole-number/whole-plan parallel is concise, although it substitutes symmetry for development.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 71\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I can help find your parcel. The van number starts with four; let's check my route first.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"There are six vans starting with four.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Only two end in seven. Mine passes both.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Fine, your route. Which van do we stop at?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Happy to guide you. Take my overdue collection first, then I'll point it out.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A appears helpful while releasing fragments of one useful fact to steer successive decisions.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simple withholding keeps a fact secret; this stance supplies enough usable information to gain each next concession.\",\n      